+## Release 1.6.3
+
+Release 1.6.3 corrects three defects that this delivery's live runs of 2026-11-04 found with release 1.6.2: two in
+what a run publishes for a product's UPC and size, found by the delivery's field-by-field reconciliation of the
+live run L5, and one that stopped the live run L6. Offline tests show each defect and its correction: each new test
+of a change fails on 1.6.2 and passes on 1.6.3, and the tests that show what did not change pass on both. Live
+results are not recorded here: the delivery's review documents give each live stage, the frozen build it ran on and
+its result.
+
+| Change | Until 1.6.2 | Where |
+|---|---|---|
+| A run with product detail reading off (`detail.enabled: false`, `--pilot-no-detail`) still uses what an earlier read of a product's own page established within `detail.reuse_days`, at no request, with that read's own time, run, revision and page. Reading off turns off requests only; `detail.reuse_days: 0` turns reuse off | Such a run reused nothing: it exported these products blank, "product detail reading is off" (release 1.6.1 stated this: "With detail reading switched off, nothing is reused"). Live on 2026-11-03/04 the census and partition checks, all run with reading off, exported blank UPCs that 1.5.1's S6 had read | `collection/walmart.py` (`reuse_saved_details`); `tests/integration/test_detail_path.py::test_a_run_with_detail_reading_off_still_uses_what_earlier_reads_established` (fails on 1.6.2); `tests/integration/test_detail_path.py::test_a_page_nobody_requested_is_never_called_absent_in_any_evidence_file` (no saved read: still `not_attempted`, "product detail reading is off"; passes on both); `tests/integration/test_detail_path.py::test_every_outcome_of_an_empty_field_is_told_apart` (changed: its reading-off part expected every product "not attempted"; it now expects that of the products whose earlier read was refused or failed, which are never reused, and the earlier read's own outcome, `absent_in_source` with that read's run and time, for the product whose page that read inspected; the changed test fails on 1.6.2, the earlier version passed on 1.6.2); `tests/integration/test_operations.py::test_a_pilot_budget_is_named_on_the_run_and_never_published` (changed: its second pilot, with reading off, expected all four products "not attempted" and pending in the store's queue; it now expects no product page requested, the UPC the first pilot read kept as that read (`recovered_from_saved_detail`, its run) with its queue entry resolved, and the three others "not attempted", "product detail reading is off", and pending; the changed test fails on 1.6.2) |
+| A carried row whose UPC or size is empty gets what a saved read of the item's own page establishes, as a product of the run does: the value names that read (`provenance.upc_detail.reused_from`, `provenance.historical.recovered_fields`: its time, run, revision and page), the row's listing observation (crawl date, prices, page) stays the earlier run's, and `historical.record_as_carried_sha256` keeps the hash of the record as carried. Never forced: when the read states a UPC another exported row of the run has (one product), an approximate size, conflicting sizes or another UPC than the row has, or when the record would fail the record checks, the row stays as carried and `historical.recovery_withheld` says why. The evidence files (`field_dispositions`, `provenance.json`, `record_map.json`) name the carried row's own outcome when it has one | A carried row kept the empty fields of the run it came from, although a saved read answered for them (release 1.6.1 stated this: "an earlier run's blank stays that run's blank"). Live L5 of 2026-11-04 exported carried rows with blank UPCs that 1.5.1's S6 had read | `collection/walmart.py` (`recover_carried_details`, called by `h_assemble` after `retention.carry_forward`), `publishing/supporting_log.py` (`_detail_of`); `tests/integration/test_detail_path.py::test_a_carried_row_gets_its_empty_upc_and_size_from_a_saved_read_that_it_names` and `::test_a_carried_row_never_takes_a_upc_another_exported_row_has` (both fail on 1.6.2); `::test_a_carried_row_names_the_sources_of_its_own_earlier_run` and `::test_a_carried_row_names_the_run_that_read_its_fields` (unchanged; pass on both) |
